mali400: take BUILD_DATE from SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, not the wall clock

The vendor Mali Kbuild composes a VERSION_STRINGS blob that is compiled into
the driver, and one of its entries is `BUILD_DATE=$(shell date)`. That is a
make-time shell call, so no KBUILD_BUILD_* value and no SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
handling in the compiler reaches it: two builds of one unchanged tree embed
their own wall clocks and the Image differs.

Measured under RFCT-343: two `--no-cache` builds sixteen minutes apart embedded
`BUILD_DATE=Mon Sep  7 14:38:57 UTC 2026` and `... 14:55:18 UTC 2026`, four
differing bytes, which then moved the GNU build-id -- a hash of the linked
image -- by a further twenty.

`$${SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH:-0}` rather than `$(SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH)`: the `$$` leaves
the expansion to the shell, so a build that does not set the variable gets the
epoch rather than a `date` error and an empty string. This board's builder sets
it; the fallback is so the vendor tree stays buildable without it.

The same file passes `-Wno-date-time` (line 194), which is why the driver's
`__DATE__`/`__TIME__` uses compile at all in a tree whose top-level Kbuild sets
`-Werror=date-time`. Those two are fixed by SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH in the compiler
and need no patch; this one is not reachable that way.

WHY ONE PATCH IS ENOUGH, and it is an enumeration rather than the observation
that a pair matched. A same-day experiment cannot see a date-only string, so
the pinned tree was searched whole:

  * `$(shell date` over every Makefile, Kbuild and *.mk: ONE hit, this line.
  * `__DATE__`/`__TIME__` over every .c, .h and .S: twenty files -- this
    driver, its ump/umplock siblings, an nvp6158 tuner, a goodix tool, bcmdhd
    (which this board disables), acpica, and thirteen AMD GPU register headers.
    Every one of them is a cpp macro, so SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH covers all twenty
    whether or not this config compiles them.

--- a/drivers/gpu/arm/mali400/mali/Kbuild
+++ b/drivers/gpu/arm/mali400/mali/Kbuild
@@ -231,7 +231,7 @@
 VERSION_STRINGS += REVISION=$(DRIVER_REV)
 VERSION_STRINGS += CHANGED_REVISION=$(CHANGED_REVISION)
 VERSION_STRINGS += CHANGE_DATE=$(CHANGE_DATE)
-VERSION_STRINGS += BUILD_DATE=$(shell date)
+VERSION_STRINGS += BUILD_DATE=$(shell date -u -d "@$${SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH:-0}")
 ifdef CONFIG_MALI400_DEBUG
 VERSION_STRINGS += BUILD=debug
 else
